## Mandatory During-Session Protocol

When meaningful decisions occur, the IDE/agent SHOULD track:

- architecture updates
- contract/API changes
- state strategy changes (React Query/Zustand boundaries)
- feature scope changes versus initial plan

If scope changes significantly, note it for end-of-session docs update.

---

## Mandatory End-of-Session Protocol

Before ending a session, the IDE/agent MUST update:

1. `docs.md`
   - `Current Session Snapshot`
   - `Completed This Session`
   - `Open Tasks (Next)`
   - `Decisions / Risks Updated`

2. `ROADMAP.md`
   - progress checkboxes/status for touched phases
   - any milestone/task status changed during session

### End-of-session hard rule

- A session is not considered complete until both `docs.md` and `ROADMAP.md` are synchronized with actual work.
- If no status changed, explicitly record that no roadmap/status update was required.

---

## Conflict Resolution Rule

If implementation differs from existing docs:

1. Keep code as source of truth.
2. Update docs to match shipped behavior.
3. Add short note in `Decisions / Risks Updated` explaining the change.

---

## Lightweight Session Checklist

Use this checklist for every session:

- [ ] Read `ROADMAP.md`
- [ ] Read `docs.md`
- [ ] Align planned scope with roadmap
- [ ] Implement task
- [ ] Update `docs.md` snapshot/progress/risks
- [ ] Update `ROADMAP.md` progress
- [ ] Verify docs reflect actual code state

